#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:167
msgid ""
"In route handlers, ``cookies``, ``headers``, ``query`` and ``scope`` can "
"also be accessed through the request, e.g. ``request.headers``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:170
msgid ":ref:`handler-function-kwargs`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:14
msgid ""
"A websocket connection attempt to a path that only has HTTP route handlers "
"raised an unhandled ``KeyError``, resulting in a ``500 - Internal Server "
"Error`` and a logged traceback. It now returns a ``400 - Bad Request``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:23
msgid ""
"Serialize subscription changes and consume notifications in a background "
"task so dynamic ``LISTEN`` and ``UNLISTEN`` operations no longer contend "
"with the listener. :class:`~litestar.channels.backends.psycopg."
"PsycoPgChannelsBackend` now requires psycopg 3.2.4 or newer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:33
msgid ""
":class:`~litestar.channels.backends.redis.RedisChannelsPubSubBackend` called "
"``PubSub.reset()`` on shutdown, which is deprecated since redis-py 5.0.1 and "
"emitted a :exc:`DeprecationWarning`. It now calls ``PubSub.aclose()``, "
"falling back to ``reset()`` on older redis-py versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:43
msgid ""
"``LitestarGroup.add_command()`` ignored its ``name`` argument and always "
"registered a command under the command's own name. The name is now passed on "
"to Click, so CLI commands loaded from plugin entry points are registered "
"under the entry point's name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:53
msgid ""
"Metadata declared with ``Parameter()`` or ``Body()``, such as a title, "
"description, examples or constraints, was not rendered where the field is "
"used if the field's type is rendered as a reference to a component schema, "
"such as a model, an enum or a DTO. For example, ``Body(examples=[...])`` on "
"a ``data`` parameter typed as a model did not show up in the request body "
"schema."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:59
msgid ""
"Such fields are now rendered as ``{\"allOf\": [{\"$ref\": ...}], ...}``, "
"with the metadata next to the reference. Fields without metadata are still "
"rendered as a plain ``$ref``. ``schema_extra`` is still applied to the "
"component schema."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:68
msgid ""
":class:`~litestar.channels.backends.asyncpg.AsyncPgChannelsBackend` uses a "
"single connection to add and remove listeners. Concurrent subscription "
"changes could overlap on that connection and raise ``InterfaceError: another "
"operation is in progress``. Subscription changes and startup and shutdown of "
"the backend are now serialized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:74
msgid ""
"Subscriptions are now cleared on shutdown, which allows reusing a backend "
"instance after it has been shut down."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:81
msgid ""
":class:`OpenAPIFormat.IRI <litestar.openapi.spec.OpenAPIFormat>` had the "
"value ``\"iri-reference\"``, the same as ``OpenAPIFormat.IRI_REFERENCE``. It "
"now has the value ``\"iri\"``, as defined by the `JSON Schema specification "
"<https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-bhutton-json-schema-"
"validation-00#section-7.3.5>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:90
msgid ""
":meth:`MutableScopeHeaders.getall() <litestar.datastructures."
"MutableScopeHeaders.getall>` raised a :exc:`KeyError` for a missing header "
"when an empty list was passed as ``default``, instead of returning it. In "
"addition, the :exc:`KeyError` raised by ``getall()`` and by item access for "
"a missing header now contains the header name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:101
msgid ""
"The routing cache was a class-level ``lru_cache``, which kept every router, "
"and through it every :class:`~litestar.app.Litestar` instance and its state, "
"alive for the lifetime of the process. This mainly affected processes that "
"create many applications, such as test suites. The cache is now created per "
"router, so an application can be garbage collected once it is no longer "
"referenced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:112
msgid ""
"OpenAPI response descriptions generated from exception class names split the "
"name before every capital letter, so ``InvalidAPIKeyError`` was rendered as "
"``Invalid A P I Key Error``. Consecutive capital letters are now kept "
"together, rendering ``Invalid API Key Error``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:122
msgid ""
"A ``multipart/form-data`` request whose ``Content-Type`` header has no "
"``boundary`` parameter was passed to the multipart parser with an empty "
"boundary. Such requests are now rejected with a ``400 - Bad Request``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:218
msgid ""
"Deprecate implicitly declaring dependencies. Instead, dependencies should be "
"explicitly declared with :data:`~litestar.di.NamedDependency`. Not doing so "
"will raise a :exc:`DeprecationWarning`. Implicitly declared dependencies "
"will be removed in Litestar 3.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:223
msgid ":doc:`/topics/explicit_declarations`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:182
msgid ""
"Fields typed as ``T | None`` (nullable) without a default value are now "
"correctly included in the OpenAPI schema's ``required`` array. Previously, "
"Litestar conflated nullability (the type can be ``None``) with optionality "
"(having a default value), causing the generated schema to diverge from the "
"OpenAPI 3.1.0 specification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:187
msgid ""
"This affected all model types: dataclasses, msgspec Structs, attrs classes, "
"and Pydantic models. For example, a field ``name: int | None`` with no "
"default was previously excluded from ``required``; it is now correctly "
"included."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:191
msgid ""
"Runtime request validation behavior is unchanged; nullable parameters "
"without defaults were already enforced as required at the validation layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:198
msgid ""
"When ``data`` was declared in a dependency function but not in the handler, "
"the request body was missing from the OpenAPI schema:"
