#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:425
msgid "Given:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:428
msgid ""
"@get(\"/\")\n"
"async def handler(one: str, two: str) -> None:\n"
"    pass\n"
"\n"
"router = Router(\"/{two:str}\", route_handlers=[handler])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:435
msgid ""
"``one`` is implicitly created as a query parameter, while ``two`` is a path "
"parameter declared on the router. Including ``handler`` in a different "
"context *without* that path parameter would implicitly treat ``two`` as a "
"query parameter as well. Using explicit markers, the source of each "
"parameter is clear and errors can be caught earlier:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:442
msgid ""
"@get(\"/\")\n"
"async def handler(one: FromQuery[str], two: FromPath[str]) -> None:\n"
"    pass\n"
"\n"
"router = Router(\"/{two:str}\", route_handlers=[handler])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:451
msgid ""
"Replace unmarked query / path parameters in handler and dependency "
"signatures with ``FromQuery[<type>]``/ ``FromPath[<type]`` markers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:453
msgid "Replace ``Parameter(query=...)`` with ``QueryParameter(name=...)``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:454
msgid "Replace ``Parameter(header=...)`` with ``HeaderParameter(name=...)``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:455
msgid "Replace ``Parameter(cookie=...)`` with ``CookieParameter(name=...)``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:456
msgid ""
"Hoist defaults: ``param: int = Parameter(default=\"x\")`` -> ``param: "
"FromQuery[int] = \"x\"``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:460
msgid ":doc:`/usage/routing/parameters`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:344
msgid ""
"Fix a CSRF vulnerability due to an unescaped ``csrf_input`` tag provided by "
"Litestar. When using ``CSRFConfig`` and providing the CSRF token via a "
"cookie, the cookie value was not properly escaped, which could lead to an "
"attacker being able to craft a cookie containing malicious HTML, which would "
"be rendered on the client side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:466
msgid ""
"Fix :meth:`~litestar.security.jwt.Token.decode` leaking :exc:`KeyError` or :"
"exc:`TypeError` when required claims (``sub``, ``exp``, ``iat``) are missing "
"or malformed and claim verification is disabled. Decoding now raises :exc:"
"`~litestar.exceptions.NotAuthorizedException` consistently in these cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:477
msgid ""
"Fix a regression introduced in 2.18.0 (#4271) where an empty file input in a "
"multipart form would arrive as an empty string instead of ``None``, causing "
"a ``400`` validation error for ``Optional[UploadFile]`` fields. Empty file "
"inputs annotated as ``Optional[UploadFile]`` are now converted to ``None`` "
"before reaching the conversion layer, matching the semantics of \"no file "
"selected\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:489
msgid ""
"Fix a :exc:`KeyError` raised when a msgspec ``Struct`` used as a DTO "
"contains a ``ClassVar`` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:496
msgid ""
"Fix a data race in :class:`~litestar.middleware.rate_limit."
"RateLimitMiddleware` where ``retrieve_cached_history`` and "
"``set_cached_history`` could interleave between coroutines. Both calls now "
"execute under the same :class:`anyio.Lock`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:506
msgid ""
"Remove an unreachable branch in :class:`~litestar.middleware.rate_limit."
"RateLimitMiddleware`. ``reset`` is set to ``now + duration``, and the "
"surrounding ``while`` loop already removes all items where ``reset <= now``, "
"so the removed code path could never trigger."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:517
msgid ""
"Fix OpenAPI schema generation to emit ``string`` for :class:`decimal."
"Decimal` fields instead of ``number``, matching the default string "
"serialization used by msgspec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:526
msgid ""
"Fix OpenAPI schema generation to include ``minItems``/``maxItems`` for "
"``Annotated[list[T], Meta(min_length=N)]`` and similar collection types on "
"msgspec ``Struct`` fields. Previously, length constraints were extracted "
"only for string and bytes types, leaving collection length metadata absent "
"from the generated schema even though runtime validation worked correctly. "
"The fix covers ``ListType``, ``SetType``, ``FrozenSetType``, and "
"``VarTupleType``, and adds a branch for ``msgspec.Meta`` (which is not a "
"subclass of ``annotated_types``) in the type extractor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:541
msgid ""
"Remove the content-length integrity check in :meth:`~litestar.connection."
"Request.stream` that raised ``ClientException(\"Malformed request\")`` when "
"streamed bytes exceeded the ``Content-Length`` header. This check broke when "
"request decompression middleware wrapped the ASGI ``receive`` function, "
"since the decompressed body is legitimately larger than the wire-format "
"``Content-Length``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:548
msgid ""
"Body size enforcement now relies on ``request_max_body_size`` "
"unconditionally, returning a ``413`` for oversized bodies. Content-length "
"validation at the transport layer remains the responsibility of the ASGI "
"server. The previous ``if``/``elif`` structure also meant that "
"``request_max_body_size`` enforcement was unreachable when ``Content-"
"Length`` was set; this is now corrected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:564
msgid ""
"Fix a bug where DTOs with a ``__schema_name__`` and nested models, the "
"nested model's ``$ref`` wrongly pointed to the parent's custom schema name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:572
msgid ""
"Fix a bug in the DTO codegen backend that would result in a :exc:`TypeError` "
"when a value for a deeply nested, optional field was missing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:593
msgid ""
