"A bug was fixed that resulted in exception occurring in the outermost "
"application layer not being captured under the current request span, which "
"led to incomplete traces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2034
msgid ""
"Fix a bug that would cause :class:`~litestar.middleware.csrf.CSRFMiddleware` "
"to set a cookie (which would not be used subsequently) on routes it had been "
"excluded from via a path pattern."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2043
msgid ""
"Ensure that adding signature types to ``signature_namespace`` and "
"``signature_types`` behaves the same way when a name was already present in "
"the namespace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2047
msgid ""
"Both will now issue a warning if a name is being overwritten with a "
"different type. If a name is registered again for the same type, no warning "
"will be given."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2052
msgid ""
"You can disable this warning globally by setting "
"``LITESTAR_WARN_SIGNATURE_NAMESPACE_OVERRIDE=0`` in your environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2062
msgid "Allow ``mkdir`` True when creating a file store."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2069
msgid ""
"Provide a way in the ``logging_module`` to switch easily from ``logging`` to "
"``picologging``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2075
msgid "Add handler name to exceptions raise by ``_validate_handler_function``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2082
msgid ""
"Adds parameters in pydantic plugin to support strict validation and all the "
"``model_dump`` args"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2089
msgid ""
"Ensures that the functions used by the signature model itself do not "
"interfere with the signature model created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2096
msgid ""
"Resolves infinite loop in schema generation when a model has an Annotated "
"``NewType``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2102
msgid ""
"Currently, the ``FlashPlugin`` expects the ``request`` parameter to be a "
"type of ``Request``.  However, there's no reason it can't use the parent "
"class ``ASGIConnection``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2104
msgid ""
"Doing this, allows for flash to be called in guards that expect an "
"``ASGIConnection`` instead of ``Request``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2107
msgid ""
"def requires_active_user(connection: ASGIConnection, _: BaseRouteHandler) -> "
"None:\n"
"    if connection.user.is_active:\n"
"        return\n"
"    msg = \"Your user account is inactive.\"\n"
"    flash(connection, msg, category=\"error\")\n"
"    raise PermissionDeniedException(msg)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2120
msgid ""
"Fix a bug where the validation of the return annotation for the ``head`` "
"route handler was too strict and would not allow returning a "
"``Response[None]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2130
msgid ""
"Add ``OPTIONS`` to the default safe methods for :class:`~litestar.config."
"csrf.CSRFConfig`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2137
msgid ""
"Adding new extraction function for prometheus metrics to avoid high "
"cardinality issue in prometheus, eg having metrics ``GET /v1/users/{id}`` is "
"preferable over ``GET /v1/users/1``, ``GET /v1/users/2,GET /v1/users/3``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2141
msgid ""
"More info about prometheus high cardinality https://grafana.com/"
"blog/2022/02/15/what-are-cardinality-spikes-and-why-do-they-matter/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2148
msgid ""
"Fix a bug that caused :meth:`~litestar.testing.TestClient."
"websocket_connect` / :meth:`~litestar.testing.AsyncTestClient."
"websocket_connect` to not respect the ``base_url`` set in the client's "
"constructor, and instead would use the static ``ws://testerver`` URL as a "
"base."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2153
msgid ""
"Also removes most of the test client code as it was unneeded and in the way "
"of this fix :)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2156
msgid ""
"Explanation for the last part: All the extra code we had was just proxying "
"method calls to the ``httpx.Client`` / ``httpx.AsyncClient``, while altering "
"the base URL. Since we already set the base URL on the httpx Client's "
"superclass instance, which in turn does this merging internally, this step "
"isn't needed at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2167
msgid ""
"Fix an issue where there was a deprecation warning emitted by all route "
"handler decorators. This warning was introduced in ``2.9.0`` to warn about "
"the upcoming deprecation, but should have only applied to user subclasses of "
"the handler classes, and not the built-in ones (``get``, ``post``, etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2177
msgid ""
"Don't call ``rich_click.patch`` if ``rich_click`` is installed. As this "
"monkey patches click globally, it can introduce unwanted side effects. "
"Instead, use conditional imports to refer to the correct library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2181
msgid ""
"External libraries will still be able to make use of ``rich_click`` "
"implicitly when it's installed by inheriting from ``LitestarGroup`` / "
"``LitestarExtensionGroup``, which they will by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2190
msgid ""
"When encountering a :class:`typing.NewType` during OpenAPI schema "
"generation, we currently treat it as an opaque type. This PR changes the "
"behaviour such that :class`typing.NewType`s are always unwrapped during "
"schema generation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2198
msgid ""
"When an handler raises an exception and exception handler returns a Response "
"with a model (e.g. pydantic) object, ensure that object can be encoded as "
"when returning data from a regular handler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2495
msgid "Add async ``websocket_connect`` to ``AsyncTestClient``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2504
msgid ""
"Implement ``SecretString`` and ``SecretBytes`` data structures to hide "
"sensitive data in tracebacks, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2511
msgid ""
"Deprecation for the 2.x release line of the semantic route handler classes "
"removed in #3436."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2210
msgid ""
"An exception raised within an asgi lifespan context manager would result in "
"a \"lifespan.startup.failed\" message being sent after we've already sent a "
"\"lifespan.startup.complete\" message. This would cause uvicorn to raise a "
"``STATE_TRANSITION_ERROR`` assertion error due to their check for that "
"condition , if asgi lifespan is forced (i.e., with ``$ uvicorn test_apps."
"test_app:app --lifespan on``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2215
msgid "E.g.,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2217
msgid ""
"During handling of the above exception, another exception occurred:\n"
"\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"  File \"/home/peter/.local/share/pdm/venvs/litestar-dj-FOhMr-3.8/lib/"
"python3.8/site-packages/uvicorn/lifespan/on.py\", line 86, in main\n"
"    await app(scope, self.receive, self.send)\n"
"  File \"/home/peter/.local/share/pdm/venvs/litestar-dj-FOhMr-3.8/lib/"
"python3.8/site-packages/uvicorn/middleware/proxy_headers.py\", line 69, in "
"__call__\n"
"    return await self.app(scope, receive, send)\n"
"  File \"/home/peter/PycharmProjects/litestar/litestar/app.py\", line 568, "
"in __call__\n"
"    await self.asgi_router.lifespan(receive=receive, send=send)  # type: "
"ignore[arg-type]\n"
"  File \"/home/peter/PycharmProjects/litestar/litestar/_asgi/asgi_router."
"py\", line 180, in lifespan\n"
"    await send(failure_message)\n"
"  File \"/home/peter/.local/share/pdm/venvs/litestar-dj-FOhMr-3.8/lib/"
"python3.8/site-packages/uvicorn/lifespan/on.py\", line 116, in send\n"
"    assert not self.startup_event.is_set(), STATE_TRANSITION_ERROR\n"
"AssertionError: Got invalid state transition on lifespan protocol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2234
msgid ""
"This PR modifies ``ASGIRouter.lifespan()`` so that it sends a shutdown "
"failure message if we've already confirmed startup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2241
msgid ""
"Fix a bug introduced in #3296 where it failed to take into account that the "
"``pydantic_v2`` variable could be ``Empty``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2250
msgid ""
"Fixes an :exc`ImproperlyConfiguredException` where an app that explicitly "
"registers an ``OpenAPIController`` on the application, and implicitly uses "
"the OpenAPI router via the `OpenAPIConfig` object. This was caused by the "
"two different handlers being given the same name as defined in ``litestar."
"constants``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2254
msgid ""
"PR adds a distinct name for use by the handler that serves ``openapi.json`` "
"on the controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2262
msgid ""
"Fixes bug with Pydantic V1 environment test where the test was run against "
"v2. Adds assertion for version to the test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2264
msgid ""
"Fixes a bug exposed by above that relied on pydantic not having ``v1`` in "
"the package namespace if ``v1`` is installed. This doesn't hold true after "
"pydantic's ``1.10.15`` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2273
#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2537
msgid ""
"Fix schema generated for DTOs where the supported type is wrapped in a "
"generic outer type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2276
msgid ""
"Prior behavior of using the ``backend.annotation`` as the basis for "
"generating the openapi schema for the represented type is not applicable for "
"the case where the DTO supported type is wrapped in a generic outer object. "
"In that case ``backend.annotation`` only represents the type of the "
"attribute on the generic type that holds the DTO supported type annotation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2281
msgid ""
"This change detects the case where we unwrap an outer generic type, and "
"rebuilds the generic annotation in a manner appropriate for schema "
"generation, before generating the schema for the annotation. It does this by "
"substituting the DTOs transfer model for the original model in the original "
"annotations type arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2290
msgid ""
"We now only issue a single warning for the case where a default value is "
"supplied via ``Parameter()`` and not via a regular signature default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2299
#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2551
msgid ""
"Consider parameters defined in handler dependencies in order to determine if "
"a path parameter has been consumed for openapi generation purposes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2302
msgid ""
"Fixes an issue where path parameters not consumed by the handler, but "
"consumed by dependencies would cause an :exc`ImproperlyConfiguredException`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2310
#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2566
msgid ""
"Exclude the \"name\" and \"in\" fields from openapi schema generated for "
"headers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2312
msgid ""
"Add ``BaseSchemaObject._iter_fields()``  method that allows schema types to "
"define the fields that should be included in their openapi schema "
"representation and override that method for ``OpenAPIHeader``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2321
msgid ""
"Fix import from ``contrib.minijinja`` without handling for case where "
"dependency is not installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2329
#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2580
msgid ""
"Fix an issue where a regular handler under a mounted asgi app would prevent "
"a request from routing through the mounted application if the request path "
"contained the path of the regular handler as a substring."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2337
msgid ""
"Fix and issue with converting ``StructLoggingConfig`` to dict during call to "
"``configure()`` when the config object has a custom logger factory that "
"references a ``TextIO`` object, which cannot be pickled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2346
#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2595
msgid ""
"Fix an issue where the connection session cookie is not cleared if the "
"response session is stored across multiple cookies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2354
msgid "Fix an issue where flashed messages were not shown after a redirect"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2361
msgid ""
"A ``Sequence[UploadFile] | None`` would not pass validation when a single "
"value was provided for a structured type, e.g. dataclass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2369
msgid ""
"Fix issue where a pydantic v1 field annotation is wrapped with ``Optional`` "
"if it is marked not required, but has a default value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2376
msgid ""
"Prevent the app's exception handler middleware from starting a response "
"after one has already started."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2379
msgid ""
"When something in the middleware stack raises an exception after a \"http."
"response.start\" message has already been sent, we end up with long "
"exception chains that obfuscate the original exception."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2383
msgid ""
"This change implements tracking of when a response has started, and if so, "
"we immediately raise the exception instead of sending it through the usual "
"exception handling code path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2392
msgid ""
"Prevent logging middleware from failing with a :exc:`KeyError` when a "
"response sends multiple \"http.response.body\" messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2400
msgid ""
"Added handling for transferring data from a transfer model, to a DTO "
"supported instance when the DTO supported type is nested in a mapping."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2403
msgid "I.e, handles this case:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2406
msgid ""
"@dataclass\n"
"class NestedDC:\n"
"    a: int\n"
"    b: str\n"
"\n"
"@dataclass\n"
"class DC:\n"
"    nested_mapping: Dict[str, NestedDC]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2421
msgid ""
"Fixes issue where a ``BodyKwarg`` instance provided as metadata to a data "
"type annotation was ignored for OpenAPI schema generation when the data type "
"is managed by a DTO."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2429
msgid ""
"Fix a bug that would lead to a :exc:`TypeError` when subscribed generics "
"were used in a route handler signature and subject to validation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2433
msgid ""
"from typing import Generic, TypeVar\n"
"from litestar import get\n"
"from litestar.testing import create_test_client\n"
"\n"
"T = TypeVar(\"T\")\n"
"\n"
"class Foo(Generic[T]):\n"
"    pass\n"
"\n"
"async def provide_foo() -> Foo[str]:\n"
"    return Foo()\n"
"\n"
"@get(\"/\", dependencies={\"foo\": provide_foo})\n"
"async def something(foo: Foo[str]) -> None:\n"
"    return None\n"
"\n"
"with create_test_client([something]) as client:\n"
"    client.get(\"/\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2459
msgid ""
"Exclude static file routes created with ``create_static_files_router`` from "
"the OpenAPI schema by default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2466
msgid ""
"When mounting an app, path resolution uses ``re.search`` instead or ``re."
"match``, thus mounted app matches any path which contains mount path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2474
msgid ""
"The wording of the log message, when logging an exception, has been updated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2475
msgid ""
"For structlog, the ``traceback`` field in the log message (which contained a "
"truncated stacktrace) has been removed. The ``exception`` field is still "
"around and contains the full stacktrace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2477
msgid ""
"The option ``traceback_line_limit`` has been deprecated. The value is now "
"ignored, the full stacktrace will be logged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:2484
msgid ""
"Fix an issue in the OpenAPI YAML schema dump logic of ``OpenAPIController`` "
