#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:3516
msgid ""
"Fix a bug that would lead to a :exc:`SerializationException` when custom "
"types were present in an exception response handled by the built-in "
"exception handlers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:3521
msgid ""
"class Foo:\n"
"    pass\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"@get()\n"
"def handler() -> None:\n"
"    raise ValidationException(extra={\"foo\": Foo(\"bar\")})\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"app = Litestar(route_handlers=[handler], type_encoders={Foo: lambda foo: "
"\"foo\"})"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:3533
msgid ""
"The cause was that, in examples like the one shown above, ``type_encoders`` "
"were not resolved properly from all layers by the exception handling "
"middleware, causing the serializer to throw an exception for an unknown type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:3542
msgid ""
"The ``event_type`` set within an SSE returned from a handler would revert "
"back to a default after the first message sent:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:3546
msgid ""
"@get(\"/stream\")\n"
"async def stream(self) -> ServerSentEvent:\n"
"    async def gen() -> AsyncGenerator[str, None]:\n"
"        c = 0\n"
"        while True:\n"
"            yield f\"<div>{c}</div>\\n\"\n"
"            c += 1\n"
"\n"
"    return ServerSentEvent(gen(), event_type=\"my_event\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:3557
msgid ""
"In this example, the event type would only be ``my_event`` for the first "
"message, and fall back to a default afterwards. The implementation has been "
"fixed and will now continue sending the set event type for all messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:3566
msgid ""
"Uploading a single file when the validation target allowed multiple would "
"cause a :exc:`ValidationException`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:3570
msgid ""
"class FileUpload(Struct):\n"
"    files: list[UploadFile]\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"@post(path=\"/\")\n"
"async def upload_files_object(\n"
"    data: Annotated[FileUpload, Body(media_type=RequestEncodingType."
"MULTI_PART)]\n"
") -> list[str]:\n"
"    pass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:3582
msgid ""
"This could would only allow for 2 or more files to be sent, and otherwise "
"throw an exception."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:3589
msgid ""
"Fix a bug that would allow some channels backend to receive messages from a "
"channel it just unsubscribed from, for a short period of time, due to how "
"the different brokers handle unsubscribes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:3594
msgid ""
"await backend.subscribe([\"foo\", \"bar\"])  # subscribe to two channels\n"
"await backend.publish(\n"
"    b\"something\", [\"foo\"]\n"
")  # publish a message to a channel we're subscribed to\n"
"\n"
"# start the stream after publishing. Depending on the backend\n"
"# the previously published message might be in the stream\n"
"event_generator = backend.stream_events()\n"
"\n"
"# unsubscribe from the channel we previously published to\n"
"await backend.unsubscribe([\"foo\"])\n"
"\n"
"# this should block, as we expect messages from channels\n"
"# we unsubscribed from to not appear in the stream anymore\n"
"print(anext(event_generator))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:3611
msgid ""
"Backends affected by this were in-memory, Redis PubSub and asyncpg. The "
"Redis stream and psycopg backends were not affected."
msgstr ""

