"        }\n"
"      }\n"
"    }\n"
"  ]\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4284
msgid ""
"When structlog is not installed, the request body would not get parsed and "
"shown as a byte sequence. Instead, it was serialized into a string with the "
"assumption that it is valid UTF-8. This was fixed by decoding the bytes with "
"``backslashreplace`` before displaying them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4294
msgid ""
"Fix the typing for ``ExceptionHandler`` to support subclasses of "
"``Exception``, such that code like this will type check properly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4298
msgid ""
"from litestar import Request, Response\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"class CustomException(Exception): ...\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def handle_exc(req: Request, exc: CustomException) -> Response: ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4312
msgid ""
"Fix a bug where an annotation such as ``tuple[str, ...]`` would cause a "
"``TypeError: '<' not supported between instances of 'NoneType' and "
"'OpenAPIType')``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4319
msgid ""
"Fix a bug that would cause high CPU loads while idling when using a "
"``ChannelsPlugin`` with the ``arbitrary_channels_allowed`` enabled and while "
"no subscriptions for any channel were active."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4328
msgid ""
"When trying to export a schema via the ``litestar schema openapi --output "
"schema.json`` making use of a non-JSON serializable type, would result in an "
"encoding error because the standard library JSON serializer was used. This "
"has been fixed by using Litestar's own JSON encoder, enabling the "
"serialization of all types supplied by the schema."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4339
msgid ""
"Existing behavior was to make the schema for every type that is a union with "
"``None`` a ``\"one_of\"`` schema, that includes ``OpenAPIType.NULL`` in the "
"``\"one_of\"`` types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4343
msgid ""
"When a ``Literal`` or ``Enum`` type is in a union with ``None``, this "
"behavior is not desirable, as we want to have ``null`` available in the list "
"of available options on the type's schema."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4347
msgid ""
"This was fixed by modifying ``Literal`` and ``Enum`` schema generation so "
"that i t can be identified that the types are in a union with ``None``, "
"allowing ``null`` to be included in ``Schema.enum`` values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4356
msgid ""
"A bug was fixed that would cause the cache for routes being overwritten by a "
"route handler on that same route with a different HTTP method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4444
msgid ""
"The CLI and all its dependencies are now included by default, to enable a "
"better and more consistent developer experience out of the box."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4447
msgid ""
"The previous ``litestar[cli]`` extra is still available for backwards "
"compatibility, but as of ``2.2.0`` it is without effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4455
msgid ""
"A new :class:`~litestar.contrib.pydantic.PydanticPlugin` has been added, "
"which can be used to configure Pydantic behaviour. Currently it supports "
"setting a ``prefer_alias`` option, which will pass the ``by_alias=True`` "
"flag to Pydantic when exporting models, as well as generate schemas "
"accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4464
msgid ""
"The YAML version of the OpenAPI schema is now available under ``/schema/"
"openapi.yml`` in addition to ``/schema/openapi.yaml``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4471
msgid ""
"A new DTO backend was introduced which speeds up the transfer process by "
"generating optimized Python code ahead of time. Testing shows that the new "
"backend is between 2.5 and 5 times faster depending on the operation and "
"data provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4476
msgid ""
"The new backend can be enabled globally for all DTOs by passing the "
"appropriate feature flag to the Litestar application:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4480
msgid ""
"from litestar import Litestar\n"
"from litestar.config.app import ExperimentalFeatures\n"
"\n"
"app = Litestar(experimental_features=[ExperimentalFeatures.DTO_CODEGEN])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4487
msgid ""
"For more information see :ref:`usage/dto/0-basic-use:Improving performance "
"with the codegen backend`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4495
msgid ""
"Error messages for missing required parameters will now also contain the "
"source of the expected parameter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4498
msgid "Before:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4500
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"status_code\": 400,\n"
"  \"detail\": \"Missing required parameter foo for url http://testerver."
"local\"\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4508
msgid "After:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4510
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"status_code\": 400,\n"
"  \"detail\": \"Missing required header parameter 'foo' for url http://"
"testerver.local\"\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4369
msgid ""
"The exception handler middleware would, when in debug mode, implicitly call "
"an object's :meth:`__bool__ <object.__bool__>`, which would lead to errors "
"if that object overloaded the operator, for example if the object in "
"question was a SQLAlchemy element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4379
msgid ""
"Some re-exports of filter and exception types from ``advanced-alchemy`` were "
"missing, causing various issues when ``advanced-alchemy`` was installed, but "
"Litestar would still use its own version of these classes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4387
msgid ""
"The ``create_engine`` method was removed in an ``advanced-alchemy`` "
"releases. This was addresses by re-adding it to the versions provided by "
"Litestar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4395
msgid ""
"The ``before_request`` would modify the return annotation of associated "
"route handlers to conform with its own return type annotation, which would "
"cause issues and unexpected behaviour when that annotation was not "
"compatible with the original one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4400
msgid ""
"This was fixed by not having the ``before_request`` handler modify the route "
"handler's signature. Users are now expected to ensure that values returned "
"from a ``before_request`` handler conform to the return type annotation of "
"the route handler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4410
msgid ""
"A previous limitation was removed that would apply compression from the :"
"class:`~litestar.middleware.compression.CompressionMiddleware` only *after* "
"a response was restored from the cache, resulting in unnecessary repeated "
"computation and increased size of the stored response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4415
msgid ""
"This was due to caching being handled on the response layer, where a "
"response object would be pickled, restored upon a cache hit and then re-"
"sent, including all middlewares."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4419
msgid ""
"The new implementation now instead applies caching on the ASGI level; "
"Individual messages sent to the ``send`` callable are cached, and later re-"
"sent. This process ensures that the compression middleware has been applied "
"before, and will be skipped when re-sending a cached response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4424
msgid ""
"In addition, this increases performance and reduces storage size even in "
"cases where no compression is applied because the slow and inefficient "
"pickle format can be avoided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4432
msgid ""
"A process was removed where Litestar would implicitly attempt to parse parts "
"of URL encoded data as JSON. This was originally added to provide some "
"performance boosts when that data was in fact meant to be JSON, but turned "
"out to be too fragile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4437
msgid "Regular data conversion / validation is unaffected by this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4525
msgid ""
":meth:`~litestar.response.Response.to_asgi_response` was passing a non-:obj:"
"`None` default value (``[]``) to ``ASGIResponse`` for ``encoded_headers``, "
"resulting in a :exc:`DeprecationWarning` being raised. This was fixed by "
"leaving the default value as :obj:`None`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4534
msgid ""
"`View the full changelog <https://github.com/litestar-org/litestar/compare/"
"v2.0.0...v2.1.0x>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4541
msgid "Make ``302`` the default ``status_code`` for redirect responses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4548
msgid ""
"Adds the :meth:`include_in_schema` option to all layers, allowing to include/"
"exclude specific routes from the generated OpenAPI schema."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4556
msgid ""
"Adds deprecation warning for unused ``app`` parameter of "
"``to_asgi_response`` as it is unused and redundant due to ``request.app`` "
"being available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4563
msgid ""
"Adds ``token_extras`` to both :func:`BaseJWTAuth.login` and :meth:"
"`BaseJWTAuth.create_token` methods, to allow the definition of the "
"``extras`` JWT field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4571
msgid ""
"Adds the ability to pass a custom Jinja2 ``Environment`` or Mako "
"``TemplateLookup`` by providing a dedicated class method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4578
msgid "Adds support for MiniJinja, a minimal Jinja2 implementation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4580
msgid ":doc:`/usage/templating`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4586
msgid ""
":class:`SQLAlchemyDTO (Advanced Alchemy) <advanced_alchemy.extensions."
"litestar.dto.SQLAlchemyDTO>` can now be configured using a separate config "
"object. This can be set using both class inheritance and `Annotated <https://"
"docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Annotated>`_:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4591
msgid ""
":class:`SQLAlchemyDTO (Advanced Alchemy) <advanced_alchemy.extensions."
"litestar.dto.SQLAlchemyDTO>` can now be configured using a separate config "
"object using ``config`` object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4591
msgid ""
"class MyModelDTO(SQLAlchemyDTO[MyModel]):\n"
"    config = SQLAlchemyDTOConfig()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4596
msgid "or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4599
msgid ""
":class:`SQLAlchemyDTO (Advanced Alchemy) <advanced_alchemy.extensions."
"litestar.dto.SQLAlchemyDTO>` can now be configured using a separate config "
"object using ``Annotated``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4599
msgid " MyModelDTO = SQLAlchemyDTO[Annotated[MyModel, SQLAlchemyDTOConfig()]]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4603
msgid ""
"The new configuration currently accepts a single attribute which is "
"``include_implicit_fields`` that has a default value of ``True``. If set to "
"to ``False``, all implicitly mapped columns will be hidden from the ``DTO``. "
"If set to ``hybrid-only``, then hybrid properties will be shown but not "
"other implicit columns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4608
msgid ""
"Finally, implicit columns that are marked with ``Mark.READ_ONLY`` or ``Mark."
"WRITE_ONLY`` will always be shown regardless of the value of "
"``include_implicit_fields``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4615
msgid ""
"Enhances the SQLALchemy repository so that you can more easily pass in "
"complex ``where`` expressions into the repository functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4617
msgid ""
"Without this, you have to override the ``statement`` parameter and it "
"separates the where conditions from the filters and the ``kwargs``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4619
msgid "Allows usage of this syntax:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4622
msgid ""
"locations, total_count = await model_service.list_and_count(\n"
"    ST_DWithin(UniqueLocation.location, geog, 1000), "
"account_id=str(account_id)\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4627
msgid "instead of the previous method of overriding the ``statement``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4630
msgid ""
"locations, total_count = await model_service.list_and_count(\n"
"    statement=select(Model).where(ST_DWithin(UniqueLocation.location, geog, "
"1000)),\n"
"    account_id=str(account_id),\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4640
msgid ""
"Converts the repository to use :func:`lambda_stmt <sqlalchemy.sql.expression."
"lambda_stmt>` instead of the normal ``select``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4647
msgid ""
"Swaps the internal SQLAlchemy repository to use the external "
"`advanced_alchemy <https://docs.advanced-alchemy.jolt.rs>`_ library "
"implementations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4654
msgid ""
"Removes leftover usages of deprecated ``ExceptionHandlerMiddleware`` debug "
"parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4661
msgid ""
"Ensures that when the Pydantic validation fails in the Pydantic DTO, a :"
"class:`ValidationException` is raised with the extras set to the errors "
"given by Pydantic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4668
msgid ""
"Sets the max width of the console to 80, to prevent the output from being "
"wrapped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4676
msgid ""
"Resolves an issue where optional path parameters caused a 500 error to be "
"raised."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4682
msgid ""
"Change to using :func:`os.replace` instead of :func:`shutil.move` for "
"renaming files, to ensure atomicity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4689
msgid ""
"Set correctly the detail attribute on :class:`LitestarException` and :class:"
"`HTTPException` regardless of whether it's passed positionally or by name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4697
msgid "Fixes :meth:`exists` method for SQLAlchemy sync and async."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4703
msgid ""
"Allows importing from ``litestar.contrib.sqlalchemy.base`` even if Pydantic "
"is not installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4710
msgid ""
"Ensures that the ``content-type`` header is not added for responses that do "
"not have a body such as responses with status code ``204 (No Content)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4717
msgid ""
"Changes the way the ``SQLAlchemyPlugin`` to now append the other plugins "
"instead of the inheritance that was previously used. This makes using the "
"``plugins.get`` function work as expected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4725
msgid ""
"Fixes a bug which caused the ``--app-dir`` option to the Litestar CLI to not "
"be propagated during autodiscovery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4731
msgid ""
"Sets the ``content-length`` header by default even if the length of the body "
"is ``0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4738
msgid ""
"Update :class:`ASGIResponse`, :class:`Response` and friends to address a few "
"issues related to headers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4740
msgid ""
"If ``encoded_headers`` were passed in at any point, they were mutated within "
"responses, leading to a growing list of headers with every response"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4741
msgid ""
"While mutating ``encoded_headers``, the checks performed to assert a value "
"was (not) already present, headers were not treated case-insensitive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4742
msgid ""
"Unnecessary work was performed while converting cookies / headers into an "
"encoded headers list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4744
msgid "This was fixed by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4746
msgid "Removing the use of and deprecate ``encoded_headers``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4747
msgid ""
"Handling headers on :class:`ASGIResponse` with :class:`MutableScopeHeaders`, "
"which allows for case-insensitive membership tests, ``.setdefault`` "
"operations, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4753
msgid "Adds an export that was overlooked for the base repo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4760
msgid ""
"Resolves issue in ``attrs``, ``msgspec`` and Pydantic for multi-part forms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4767
msgid ""
"Sets ``OPTIONS`` as the default value for ``exclude_http_methods`` in the "
"base authentication middleware class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4777
msgid ""
"Fixed a regression that caused error responses to be sent using a mismatched "
"media type, e.g. an error response from a ``text/html`` endpoint would be "
"sent as JSON."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4786
msgid ""
"Fixed a regression where setting ``Litestar.debug`` would not propagate to "
"the exception handler middleware, resulting in exception responses always "
"being sent using the initial debug value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4794
msgid ""
"Fixed a bug that would result in a ``404 - Not Found`` when requesting a "
"static file where the :attr:`~litestar.static_files.StaticFilesConfig.path` "
"was also used by a route handler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4802
msgid ""
"Add missing default values for the ``receive`` and ``send`` parameters of :"
"class:`~litestar.contrib.htmx.request.HTMXRequest`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4810
msgid ""
"Fix the behaviour of DTOs such that they will no longer access fields that "
"have been included. This behaviour would previously cause issues when these "
"attributes were either costly or impossible to access (e.g. lazy loaded "
"relationships of a SQLAlchemy model)."
