#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:6402
msgid ""
":class:`Partial <litestar.partial.Partial>` now supports constructing "
"partial models for attrs and msgspec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:6408
msgid ""
":class:`Annotated <typing.Annotated>` can now be used in route handler and "
"dependencies to specify additional information about the fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:6412
msgid ""
"@get(\"/\")\n"
"def index(param: int = Parameter(gt=5)) -> dict[str, int]: ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:6417
msgid ""
"@get(\"/\")\n"
"def index(param: Annotated[int, Parameter(gt=5)]) -> dict[str, int]: ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:6426
msgid ""
"The media type in :class:`Redirect <litestar.response.RedirectResponse>` "
"won't be forced to ``text/plain`` anymore and now supports setting arbitrary "
"media types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:6435
msgid "Fix a bug where certain annotations would cause a :exc:`NameError`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:6443
msgid ""
"Add the ``uvicorn`` package to the ``cli`` extra, as it is required "
"unconditionally"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:6451
msgid ""
"When passing ``debug=True`` to :class:`Litestar <litestar.app.Litestar>`, "
"the ``litestar`` logger would be set up in debug mode, but changing the "
"``debug`` attribute after the class had been instantiated did not update the "
"logger accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:6455
msgid ""
"This lead to a regression where the ``--debug`` flag to the CLI's ``run`` "
"command would no longer have the desired affect, as loggers would still be "
"on the ``INFO`` level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:6465
msgid ""
"A :class:`SQLAlchemyInitPlugin <litestar.contrib.sqlalchemy.plugins."
"SQLAlchemyInitPlugin>` was added, providing support for managed synchronous "
"and asynchronous sessions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:6469
msgid ":doc:`/usage/databases/sqlalchemy/index`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:6475
msgid ""
"Added support to model route handler signatures with attrs instead of "
"Pydantic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:6482
msgid ""
"Add support for manually setting status codes in the :class:"
"`RedirectResponse <litestar.response_containers.Redirect>` response "
"container. This was previously only possible by setting the ``status_code`` "
"parameter on the corresponding route handler, making dynamic redirect status "
"codes and conditional redirects using this container hard to implement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:6493
msgid ""
"Add the :class:`CACHE_FOREVER <litestar.config.response_cache."
"CACHE_FOREVER>` sentinel value, that, when passed to a route handlers "
"``cache argument``, will cause it to be cached forever, skipping the default "
"expiration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:6496
msgid ""
"Additionally, add support for setting :attr:`ResponseCacheConfig."
"default_expiration <litestar.config.response_cache.ResponseCacheConfig>` to "
"``None``, allowing to cache values indefinitely by default when setting "
"``cache=True`` on a route handler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:6504
msgid ""
"Add an :attr:`accept <litestar.connection.Request.accept>` property to :"
"class:`Request <litestar.connection.Request>`, returning the newly added :"
"class:`Accept <litestar.datastructures.headers.Accept>` header wrapper, "
"representing the requests ``Accept`` HTTP header, offering basic content "
"negotiation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:6510
msgid ":ref:`usage/responses:Content Negotiation`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:6516
msgid ""
"Add a new set of features for handling WebSockets, including automatic "
"connection handling, (de)serialization of incoming and outgoing data "
"analogous to route handlers and OOP based event dispatching."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:6520
msgid ":doc:`/usage/websockets`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:6527
msgid ""
"When using the SQLAlchemy 1 plugin, repeatedly running through the "
"application lifecycle (as done when testing an application not provided by a "
"factory function), would result in a :exc:`KeyError` on the second pass."
